 "granularity_rationale": "Articles and numbered paragraphs are the units an auditor tests a control against (e.g. GDPR art:32(1)); lettered points and sub-points are NOT listed, but references to them are accepted when their parent identifier is listed. A paragraph identifier is only listed where the paragraph carries an explicit number in the official text (single-paragraph articles get no paragraph identifier). Recitals are listed as recital:N because the purpose of the legislation is expressed there and regulators and courts cite them; annexes of Directive 2014/65/EU are listed as annex:I to annex:IV. MiFID II is a Directive and MiFIR a Regulation; both instruments are in this file because auditors test against the two together. Consolidated texts are used so inserted articles such as 16a or 27da are valid references.",
